From 9e81acda96717b39bcccd3656fc31bdb18da5a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Thompson <brandon.joseph.thompson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 10:07:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Patch: Add a window-info popout to the bar's focused title

Not knowing what's running behind a truncated or generic-looking
window title was a recurring annoyance. Clicking the title now grows
a popout off the bar edge with the window's class, workspace,
monitor, size, floating/fullscreen state, and Xwayland flag, plus the
process behind it: pid, live CPU/memory, and the full command line.
Wired into all three places BarTitle is used (the default/nacre skins
in Bar.qml and the delos island).

The window data comes from Hyprland.activeToplevel rather than the
generic ToplevelManager the title itself renders off, since only its
lastIpcObject carries pid/class/geometry. That property turned out to
be event-driven only (populated by activewindowv2 IPC events, not by
any query), so on a fresh shell start it read null until the first
focus change -- the same gap Bar.qml already seeds around for
focusedWorkspace. Seeded the same way here with a one-shot hyprctl
activewindow query, superseded the moment a live event lands.

diff --git a/docs/bar.md b/docs/bar.md
index 8a4d3cb2..f9843b19 100644
--- a/docs/bar.md
+++ b/docs/bar.md
@@ -60,7 +60,10 @@ A left group and a right group flank the centred clock:
 - **力 seal** the brand mark and launcher trigger; a bare glyph (a `BarModule`
   with `filled: false`), not a control capsule.
 - **workspaces** (`BarWorkspaces`) the skin's workspace strip.
-- **focused title** the active window's title.
+- **focused title** the active window's title; clicking it opens the
+  window-info popout (`WindowInfoPopout`) with the window's class, workspace,
+  monitor, geometry and floating/fullscreen state, and the process behind it
+  (pid, command line, live CPU/memory).
 - **clock** (`BarClock`, centred) the time; clicking opens the calendar popout.
 - **now-playing** (`BarMedia`) the track's art + title; clicking toggles play, the
   wheel nudges volume, and hovering opens the transport popout (`MediaPopout`).
